<report>
<title>Risk analysis (retrospective)</title>
<line></line>
<table>
<tr><th></th><tdfirst><subtotal>Characteristic factor:</subtotal></tdfirst><td></td></tr>
<tr><td><subtotal>Outcome:</subtotal></td><td>Present</td><td>Absent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Positive</td><td><in>aa</in></td><td><in>bb</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Negative</td><td><in>cc</in></td><td><in>dd</in></td></tr>
</table>
<line></line>
<line>Observed odds ratio = <inu>odds</inu></line>
<line>Approximate power <in>pwr</in></line>
<block name="power">
<line></line>
<line><ci>Approximate (Woolf, logit) <inu>ci</inu>% confidence interval = <inu>ci_1</inu>  to  <inu>ci_2</inu> </ci></line>
<line></line>
</block>
<line>Conditional maximum likelihood estimates:</line>
<line>Conditional estimate of odds ratio = <inu>eor</inu></line>
<line><ci>Exact Fisher <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <inu>llf</inu>  to  <inu>ulf</inu></ci></line>
<line><pval>Exact Fisher one sided <inp>p1f</inp>, two sided <inp>p2f</inp></pval></line>
<line><ci>Exact mid-P <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <inu>llm</inu>  to  <inu>ulm</inu></ci></line>
<line><pval>Exact mid-P one sided <inp>p1m</inp>, two sided <inp>p2m</inp></pval></line>
<line></line>
<block name="risk">
<line>Population exposure % = <inu>pe</inu></line>
<line>Population attributable risk % = <inu>par</inu></line>
<line><ci>Approximate <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <inu>from</inu>  to  <inu>to</inu></ci></line>
</block>
</report>